#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:1
msgid "Build Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:3
msgid ""
"This script manages a tiny [LiveReload](http://livereload.com/) server "
"implementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:6
msgid ""
"[![NPM](https://nodei.co/npm/tiny-"
"lr.png?downloads=true&stars=true)](https://nodei.co/npm/tiny-lr/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:6
msgid "NPM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:8
msgid ""
"It exposes an HTTP server and express middleware, with a very basic REST "
"API to notify the server of a particular change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:11
msgid ""
"It doesn't have any watch ability, this must be done at the build process"
" or application level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:14
msgid ""
"Instead, it exposes a very simple API to notify the server that some "
"changes have been made, then broadcasted to every connected livereload "
"client."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:26
msgid ""
"Or you can bulk the information into a POST request, with the body as a "
"JSON array of files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:34
msgid ""
"As for the livereload client, you need to install the browser extension: "
"http://feedback.livereload.com/knowledgebase/articles/86242-how-do-i"
"-install-and-use-the-browser-extensions- (**note**: you need to listen on"
" port 35729 to be able to use it with your browser extension)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:39
msgid ""
"or add the livereload script tag manually: "
"http://feedback.livereload.com/knowledgebase/articles/86180-how-do-i-add-"
"the-script-tag-manually- (and here you can choose whichever port you "
"want)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:43
msgid "Integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:45
msgid ""
"The best way to integrate the runner into your workflow is to add it as a"
" `reload` step within your build tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:60
msgid "You can define your own route and listen for a specific request:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:71
msgid "And stop the server manually:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:77
msgid ""
"This will close any websocket connection established and emit a close "
"event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:79
msgid "Middleware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:81
msgid ""
"To use as a connect / express middleware, tiny-lr needs query / "
"bodyParser middlewares prior in the stack (to handle POST requests)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:84
msgid ""
"Any handled requests ends at the tinylr level, not found and errors are "
"nexted to the rest of the stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:108
msgid ""
"The port you listen on is important, and tinylr should **always** listen "
"on the LiveReload standard one: `35729`. Otherwise, you won't be able to "
"rely on the browser extensions, though you can still use the manual "
"snippet approach."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:113
msgid ""
"You can also start two different servers, one on your app port, the other"
" listening on the LiveReload port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:116
msgid "Using grunt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:118
msgid ""
"Head over to [https://github.com/gruntjs/grunt-contrib-"
"watch](https://github.com/gruntjs/grunt-contrib-watch#live-reloading)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:120
msgid "Using make"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:122
msgid ""
"See the [make-livereload](https://github.com/mklabs/make-livereload) "
"repo. This repository defines a bin wrapper you can use and install with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:127
msgid "It bundles the same bin wrapper previously used in the tiny-lr repo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:138
msgid "Using gulp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:140
msgid "See the [gulp-livereload](https://github.com/vohof/gulp-livereload) repo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:142
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:144
msgid ""
"`livereload`    - Path to the client side lib (defaults to "
"`path.join(__dirname, '../node_modules/livereload-"
"js/dist/livereload.js')`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:145
msgid "`port`          - Livereload port (defaults to `35729`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:146
msgid ""
"`errorListener` - A callback to invoke when an error occurs (otherwise, "
"fallbacks to standard error output)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:147
msgid ""
"`handler`       - A function to use as the main request handler "
"(`function(req, res)`). When not defined, the default handler takes "
"place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:149
msgid "`app`           - An express or other middleware based HTTP server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:150
msgid "`key`           - Option to pass in to create an https server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:151
msgid "`cert`          - Option to pass in to create an https server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:152
msgid ""
"`pfx`           - Can also be used to create an https server instead of "
"`key` & `cert`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:153
msgid ""
"`liveCSS`       - LiveReload option to enable live CSS reloading "
"(defaults to true)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:154
msgid ""
"`liveImg`       - LiveReload option to enable live images reloading "
"(defaults to true)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:155
msgid "`prefix`        - Option to add prefix to all HTTP server routes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tiny-lr_readme.md:156
msgid ""
"`dashboard`     - A boolean to prevent tiny-lr from configuring a default"
" \"home\" route. Only used with the CLI (default: false)"
msgstr ""

